Cmd-click still doesn't follow `lsp_results_location` setting

Related: #61187. According to the [release note](https://zed.dev/releases/stable/1.16.1), the fix was included in the releases since v1.16.1, but this issue still presents in v1.16.1 and v1.17.0-pre.

### Reproduction steps

1. Set "LSP Result Location" to "Picker" in settings.
2. Create 3 files:

test1.ts
```ts
export interface Test1 {
	test(): void;
}
```

test2.ts
```ts
export interface Test2 {
	test(): void;
}
```

test3.ts
```ts
import type { Test1 } from "./test1";
import type { Test2 } from "./test2";

export const obj: Test1 & Test2 = {
	test: () => {},
};

console.log(obj.test);
// cmd-click -> ^^^^
```

3. Cmd-click on `test` inside the `console.log` call in `test3.ts`

### Current vs. Expected behavior

Current behavior: A multibuffer tab opened after clicking `test`.
Expected behavior: Show a picker like choosing "go to definition" in the context menu.

